module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.hand_written_seed_rust_wraps_silently_in_release

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data hand_written_seed_rust_wraps_silently_in_release: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "hand_written_seed_rust_wraps_silently_in_release" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "hand-written seed Rust wraps silently on integer overflow in release (the sibling of emitted_int_arithmetic_wraps_where_the_interpreter_refuses one layer down: that row covers arithmetic the emitter writes, this one covers arithmetic a person wrote in the seed's host Rust).",

    "INVALID STATE: a bare + - * or unary - on a Rust integer in hand-written seed Rust (cli_run, the interpreter host, required_regen_host and the rest), compiled under a [profile.release] that leaves overflow-checks off, so an overflow wraps in two's complement and computation continues on a fabricated value.",

    "HARM: silent wrongness in the binary that decides whether the corpus compiles and what the floor reports. The same code traps in dev and test, where overflow-checks is on by default, so a wrap cannot be reproduced by the ordinary local debugging route: the two profiles disagree on the program's meaning.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACT: intended wrapping in the seed is already spelled wrapping_* (hash mixing, step counters), and checked arithmetic is spelled checked_*; neither is affected by the profile flag, so the flag changes behaviour ONLY at sites whose wrap was never declared.",

    "REPAIR: overflow-checks = true in the workspace [profile.release], so every undeclared overflow panics in release as it already does in dev. Its wall-time cost is measured on CI in the landing PR rather than asserted here.",

    "RUNG: mitigatable -- the overflow now aborts loudly instead of fabricating, but nothing prevents authoring a bare operator that can overflow. CEILING: the seed shrinks toward zero (DESIGN section 7), so the terminal repair is deletion of hand-written seed Rust, not a lint over it. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: none worth building ahead of that migration."
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
